+<svg viewBox="0 0 1060 1000" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" font-family="system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif">
+  <title>How Compound V routes a request across three tiers</title>
+  <desc>A triage hook scores every change request and sorts it into one of three tiers. DIRECT implements in place on the current session with no manifest and no model of its own. SCOPED opens a manifest and run directory for the touched slice, and SCOPED+ adds a mandatory deep review plus a cross-model second opinion on sensitive paths. FULL runs the whole pipeline: recon and pre-flights, then an orchestrator and router that assign each job to Opus for judgment and review, Sonnet for junior slices and scans, or an opt-in Codex worker for large isolated builds or a second opinion. SCOPED and FULL both close through a git-diff scope gate and an Opus review before the work merges.</desc>
 
